Q1)
     Aim:

To design an optimized Linux file system layout for a **50 GB server** that manages logs, user files, and application data efficiently while preventing disk 
space exhaustion.
 File System Layout:
 Partition        Size  Purpose                       
 `/`             12 GB  OS and system files           
 `/var`          10 GB  System logs and variable data 
 `/home`         10 GB  User files                    
 `/opt`          10 GB  Application data              
 `/tmp`           4 GB  Temporary files               
 Free space       4 GB  Emergency/reserved space      
 Total  50 GB                               
 Storage Management:
The `/var` partition is restricted to 10 GB, ensuring that log files cannot consume the entire disk.
Use logrotate to automatically manage logs:
bash
sudo nano /etc/logrotate.d/system-logs
Example configuration:
```text
/var/log/*.log {
    daily
    rotate 7
    compress
    missingok
    notifempty
}
```
This will:
* Rotate logs daily.
* Keep only 7 old log files.
* Compress old logs.
* Remove older logs automatically.
Disk usage can be monitored using:
```bash
df -h
du -sh /var/log
```
If disk usage becomes high, old logs can be compressed or removed according to the retention policy.

